* Simplified behavioural model of ONE TL072 amplifier, written for circuit-tutor.
* This is NOT the Texas Instruments vendor macro-model: single dominant pole, output clamped
* 1.5 V inside each rail, no slew-rate limit. Aol = 2e5 (106 dB), GBW = 3 MHz.
* Pin order matches the registry unit_line: inp inm vcc vee out
.subckt TL072 inp inm vcc vee out
rin inp inm 1e12
cin inp inm 2p
* gain stage: 1 mA/V into 200 Mohm = 2e5, dominant pole at 15 Hz
g1 0 n1 inp inm 1m
r1 n1 0 200meg
c1 n1 0 53.05p
* output stage, limited to the rails
bout n2 0 v = max(min(v(n1), v(vcc) - 1.5), v(vee) + 1.5)
rout n2 out 75
* quiescent current, about 1.4 mA at +/-15 V
rq vcc vee 21.4k
.ends TL072
